#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supported wallboxes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS has two charge point connections side by side:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Connection\n"
"| Wallboxes in the code\n"
"| Control\n"
"\n"
"| **New charge point control (EVSE)**\n"
"| Alfen, Alpitronic, Ambibox, Bender, Hardy Barth (cPH1 and others), Heidelberg Connect, KEBA (Modbus, UDP, Core), Mennekes, Voltie\n"
"| xref:user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc[Surplus charging and phase switching], cluster, time schedule, energy optimizer\n"
"| **Older connection (EVCS)**\n"
"| ABL, Alpitronic Hypercharger, go-e (HTTP, Modbus, Charger Home), Hardy Barth, Heidelberg Energy, KEBA (KeContact, P40), Mennekes, Spelsberg SMART, Webasto Next and Unite, OCPP charging stations (server; drivers for ABL and IES Keywatt), openWB (read only)\n"
"| Control function “Controller Electric Vehicle Charging Station”, multi-charge-point management\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Some manufacturers exist in both connections. New apps in the app center use "
"EVSE control for Alfen, KEBA and Mennekes (see xref:user/devices/"
"cluster.adoc[Cluster])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "evcc"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"evcc comes with over 200 templates for “chargers” from around 185 brands, "
"including almost all common wallboxes (ABL, Alfen, Easee, go-e, Hardy Barth, "
"Heidelberg, KEBA, Mennekes, openWB, Tesla, Webasto, Zaptec and many more), "
"general routes such as OCPP, EEBus and Modbus as well as switchable sockets "
"and heat pumps or heating elements. For OpenEMS systems, there is **no** "
"template that controls a wallbox connected to OpenEMS via OpenEMS; evcc "
"always controls the wallbox directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "openWB"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openwb
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "openWB 2 controls charge points via these modules:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module\n"
"| What\n"
"\n"
"| Internal openWB\n"
"| the built-in charge point (also Duo with two charge points)\n"
"| Secondary openWB, openWB series2 satellit, openWB Pro\n"
"| other openWB devices, controlled by a central openWB\n"
"| openWB adapter for DC chargers\n"
"| DC chargers via an openWB adapter\n"
"| smartWB / EVSE-WiFi\n"
"| only third-party manufacturer with its own module\n"
"| MQTT charge point\n"
"| general charge point: openWB writes target current and phases via MQTT, an external program must pass this on to the actual wallbox\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"openWB therefore essentially controls its own hardware. Third-party "
"wallboxes can only be integrated via smartWB or via the MQTT charge point "
"with a self-built connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Charging modes in detail"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS (EVSE control)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-evse-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**No Charge**, **PV Surplus with guaranteed charge** (always at least at the "
"lowest power, surplus on top), **PV Surplus**, **Fast Charging**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-evse-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Mode fixed, via time schedule or once until unplugged (“One-Shot”). Optional "
"energy limit per charging session."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-evse-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Smart**: Time schedule entries with minimum charging amount; the energy "
"optimizer then plans (see xref:user/schedule/overview.adoc[Schedule], "
"xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[Time-of-use tariffs])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-evse-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Start after 10 to 20 seconds of sufficient surplus, pause only after about "
"one minute without surplus, then 5 minutes lock time; details on xref:user/"
"ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc[Surplus charging]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-evse-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"The older connection only has “Force charging” (with minimum power, default "
"7,360 W per phase) and “Optimized charging” (with optional minimum power), "
"plus the priority car or storage (see below). Change between charging and "
"pause after 120 or 30 seconds at the earliest."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "**Off**, **Now** (immediately at full power) and **Smart**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Smart** charges with PV surplus; with “always charge” (permanently or once "
"until unplugged), charging takes place at least at minimum current. With a "
"low electricity price below a limit, Smart charges fully (“smart charging”); "
"with high feed-in remuneration it can reduce charging. An optimizer can plan "
"start, stop and power itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Charging plan**: target SoC or energy amount by a time; evcc selects the "
"cheapest times."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Minimum SoC**: up to this vehicle SoC, fast charging always takes place; "
"**charging limit** as SoC or energy."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Switching on and off with thresholds and delay (default 1 minute to switch "
"on, 3 minutes to switch off)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Vehicle SoC comes from the vehicle cloud or the wallbox; without SoC, evcc "
"works with energy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mode\n"
"| Behavior\n"
"\n"
"| Instant charging\n"
"| immediately, optionally up to SoC or energy limit\n"
"| PV charging\n"
"| with surplus, optionally with minimum current and minimum SoC; switch on from 1,500 W surplus after 30 seconds, switch off after 60 seconds (defaults)\n"
"| Eco charging\n"
"| fully at a low price, otherwise like PV charging\n"
"| Target charging\n"
"| Target SoC or energy amount by time\n"
"| Time charging\n"
"| in fixed time windows\n"
"| Bidirectional charging\n"
"| provided for in the code\n"
"| Stop\n"
"| no charging\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"The modes are set per vehicle via “charging profiles”. Phase switching with "
"delay (default 7 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Home storage during charging"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| \n"
"| OpenEMS\n"
"| evcc\n"
"| openWB\n"
"\n"
"| Default\n"
"| **Car before storage**: charging power of the storage counts as surplus; discharging of the storage does not count\n"
"| also **car before storage**: charging power of the storage counts as surplus, discharging reduces it\n"
"| **Car before storage** (“vehicle priority”)\n"
"| Storage first\n"
"| older connection only: priority “Storage”, car only receives surplus from storage SoC 97 %\n"
"| “Storage priority up to SoC” (prioritySoc)\n"
"| “Storage priority” or a mode with minimum SoC of the storage (thresholds, defaults 50 % and 70 %)\n"
"| Using the storage for the car\n"
"| no (during surplus charging)\n"
"| “Discharge storage from SoC” (bufferSoc, bufferStartSoc), “battery boost” per charge point\n"
"| Settings for discharge and reserve power (defaults 1,500 W and 2,000 W, each can be switched off); exact effect not examined here\n"
"| Locking discharge into the car\n"
"| Storage is not discharged into the car during surplus charging anyway; with Force, storage control decides\n"
"| “Lock battery discharge” during fast charging (sets the storage to “Hold”)\n"
"| Storage control “no discharge”, “house consumption only” (only with controllable storage)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**With OpenEMS as the storage system:** evcc can set the OpenEMS storage to "
"“Hold” or “Charge” via the REST or Modbus write app (see xref:user/third-"
"party/evcc.adoc[evcc]). openWB only reads OpenEMS and therefore cannot "
"control the storage; its storage settings then only influence its own "
"calculation of the surplus (see xref:user/third-party/openwb.adoc[openWB])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load management"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**EVSE cluster:** distributes surplus to several charge points (even or by "
"priority). According to the code, it has no limit for the house connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Multi-charging point management** (older connection): protects the grid "
"connection; limit per phase, minimum power per car (default 4,500 W), order "
"of charging stations, optionally free discharge power of the storage. "
"Details on xref:user/devices/cluster.adoc[Cluster]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openems-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"Limits of wallbox and vehicle (minimum/maximum power single- and three-"
"phase) are taken into account in EVSE control."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Circuits**: Each circuit has a maximum current and/or maximum power, "
"optionally a meter and a higher-level circuit. This allows house connection, "
"sub-distribution and individual lines to be modeled. Limits can also come "
"dynamically from outside (e.g. from the grid operator)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-evcc-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "Charge points are given a **priority**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openwb-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**Meter hierarchy**: Each meter (utility meter, intermediate meter) has "
"current limits per phase (default 35 A) and optionally a power limit; the "
"charge points are located below it."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openwb-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "**Unbalanced load limitation** adjustable."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-openwb-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid "If the meter fails, a substitute power applies (default 7,000 W)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strengths and limits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| \n"
"| Strengths\n"
"| Limits\n"
"\n"
"| OpenEMS\n"
"| one system for storage, PV, heat and charging; joint planning by the energy optimizer; gentle control with lock times; runs on the energy manager itself\n"
"| fewer wallboxes; no vehicle SoC; load management for the house connection only with the older connection; two parallel charge point connections\n"
"| evcc\n"
"| very many wallboxes and vehicles; flexible storage rules; circuits; charging plans with prices\n"
"| needs its own device; only controls the storage via its interface; with OpenEMS only coarse storage control (hold/charge)\n"
"| openWB\n"
"| everything in the wallbox; well-thought-out load management with meter hierarchy and unbalanced load; many charging modes\n"
"| essentially only openWB hardware; read-only with OpenEMS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which combination?"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**OpenEMS only:** if the wallbox is supported by OpenEMS (preferably EVSE "
"connection) and no vehicle SoC is required."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**OpenEMS {plus} evcc:** if the wallbox is only supported by evcc or vehicle "
"SoC and charging plans are important. In this case, do not additionally set "
"up surplus charging in OpenEMS for this wallbox, and determine who controls "
"the storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"**OpenEMS {plus} openWB:** openWB controls itself and reads the values from "
"OpenEMS. OpenEMS can only display the openWB. For storage rules in openWB, "
"note that openWB cannot control the OpenEMS storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc
msgid ""
"The following applies in every combination: **only one system controls the "
"same wallbox**, and OpenEMS control functions (e.g. time-of-use tariff) can "
"interact with external specifications (see xref:user/third-party/"
"overview.adoc[Third-party systems on OpenEMS])."
msgstr ""
